File System Representation and Search Using BFS and DFS

Objective

To represent a file system as a graph using an adjacency matrix and search for a specified file using BFS and DFS.

Technologies Used

- C Programming
- Graph
- Adjacency Matrix
- Breadth-First Search (BFS)
- Depth-First Search (DFS)

Features

- Represents files and directories as graph nodes.
- Stores connections using an adjacency matrix.
- Displays BFS and DFS traversal orders.
- Checks whether the target file is found.

Files

- "main.c" – C source code
- "sample_input.txt" – Sample input
- "sample_output.txt" – Expected output

Conclusion

This project demonstrates how BFS and DFS can be used to search a graph representing a file system.
